Your explanation is likely correct, but the proposed `+1 or +2` assertion is too permissive.

- A case tunnel has separate outer and per-case inner terminals. Therefore, crossing the boundary naturally requires an outside connection and an inside connection?�consistent with two VI-Scripting `Wire` objects on two diagrams. The clearest published evidence is this accepted NI Community solution describing ?? outer terminal??and ?�one inner terminal per case.??[NI Community](https://forums.ni.com/t5/LabVIEW/LabvVIEW-Scripting-wiring-a-pass-through-tunnel-inside-a-case/m-p/3945608)
