Could `+2` mean an erroneous branch? Yes in principle: one LabVIEW wire may have multiple sinks. [NI wire documentation](https://www.ni.com/docs/en-AS/bundle/labview/page/using-wires-to-link-block-diagram-objects.html) But your census finding that the only sink is `String Subset.string`, combined with `ExecState 1`, makes that explanation very unlikely?�assuming the census covers both the outer and nested diagrams. `ExecState 1` proves compilability, not intended topology.

Recommended fix: accept `+2` only when topology confirms:

1. one new tunnel;
2. outer wire connects the control to the tunnel?�s outer terminal;
3. inner wire connects that tunnel?�s active-case inner terminal to `String Subset.string`;
4. neither wire has another sink.

So: **failed prediction confirmed; false alarm strongly supported.** Functional testing should confirm behavior, but topology-aware validation is safer than merely allowing either count.
